«
@@ ============================================================
@@ WBLoad — weight and balance of a loading.
@@
@@ Input:  a list of stations, one { "name" weight arm } list each.
@@         Arms are measured from the datum, positive aft; a negative
@@         weight removes a load, for instance the fuel burnt.
@@ Output: the total weight Wt, the total moment Mom and the center
@@         of gravity CG = Mom/Wt, tagged.
@@ Weights and arms may carry units, or be plain numbers in any
@@ consistent units.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → sta
  «
    sta 1 GET LIST→ DROP
    → nam wi ai
    «
      wi wi ai ×
    »
    2 sta SIZE FOR kk
      sta kk GET LIST→ DROP
      → nam wi ai
      «
        SWAP wi + SWAP wi ai × +
      »
    NEXT
    → wt mo
    «
      wt "Wt" →TAG
      mo "Mom" →TAG
      mo wt / "CG" →TAG
    »
  »
»
